-- title:
--   Level automorphism fixes the Γ₀(M') subfield when q∣ b
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and let $\zeta$ be an element of `Idx q`, that is a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $\gamma\in SL_2(\mathbb{Z})$ lie in $\Gamma_0(M')$ and satisfy $q\mid \gamma_{01}$, the upper right entry of $\gamma$. Let $g$ be a Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ belonging to `laurentBaseChange` of `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (Gamma0 M')`, i.e. to the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((X))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the coefficientwise images of the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((X))$ generated by the ratios $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_f/\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_g$ attached to modular forms $f,g$ of some weight $k$ on $\Gamma_0(M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$ and $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_g\neq 0$. Let $x$ be an element of `fieldBar q M'`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the function field of $X_H(q^2M')$ for $H$ the kernel of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, whose underlying Laurent series is $g$. Then $x$ is fixed by `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`, the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphism of `fieldBar q M'` chosen to satisfy `IsLevelAutBar q M' ζ γ` when such an automorphism exists (and the identity otherwise); that predicate requires, for all weights $k$, all forms $f,g$ on $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$ and $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,p_g\neq 0$, and every embedding $\iota:\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta)=e^{2\pi i/q}$, that $\iota$ applied coefficientwise to the image of $p_f/p_g$ under the automorphism, multiplied by the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k \mathrm{conjElem}\,q\,\gamma$, equals the $q$-expansion of $f\mid_k \mathrm{conjElem}\,q\,\gamma$.
--
--   This records the triviality of the level automorphism $\tau_\gamma$ on the subfield coming from level $M'$ when $\gamma$ is of Borel type at $q$, i.e. has upper right entry divisible by $q$: conjugating such a $\gamma$ by $\mathrm{diag}(q,1)$ again gives an element of $\Gamma_0(M')$, under which all forms of level $M'$, and hence all ratios of integral forms, are invariant. It feeds into the description of the effect of `levelAutBar` on elements of the $\Gamma_0(M')$ subfield as a $q$-power twist.
-- source:
